Package: SpatialClustering
Title: Comparative Multivariate Analysis of Spatial Clustering in Neanderthal and Anatomically Modern Human Occupations
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Amanda", "Merino-Pelaz", , "amandamerpel@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: This project provides a quantitative comparison of spatial organization in Neanderthal and Anatomically Modern Human (AMH) occupations. It applies cluster modeling to multiple Paleolithic assemblages to derive key spatial metrics and explores their relationship to cultural affiliation, site context, and other occupation features. The results highlight systematic differences in spatial compactness between cultural groups, offering new insights into the evolution of camp organization and social behavior during the Late Pleistocene.
